   Whew!  After roughly two days of programming and 10 days of debugging,
it's done!  I have noticed all the griping on Future World about the flood
of Space Empire type games lately, so here you go.
   This game is basically a re-write of an old game available on some 8-bit
Atari BBS called ROBOWARS.  If any of you have ever played it, you'll
notice I made some improvements.  I wrote this from scratch, and it is my 
first attempt at a program longer then 1 page.  But I think you'll agree
that it works great.  And NO spelling errors!  (Sheesh, how come no one can
spell any more?  Is everyone stupid or what?)  
   The object of the game is to build the best robot you can by conquering
other robots and getting money to upgrade yours.  This isn't easy though,
and the chances you'll ever be able to build an opponent for the top-notch
computer robot (or "compubot") is basically nill.  In this version I have
not released any docs for the player.  The entire game is self-explanitory,
and anyone should be able to figure it out with no problems.  If not, I'll
add some to the next release.
   
SETTING UP

Make a directory in your Pfiles called BOTZ.  Copy "Compubots",
"botzscreen", and all the files ending with the word ".compubot" into that
directory.  Then copy Warbotz into your Pfiles: root and it's set up!  It
will make any other files it needs in the BOTZ directory (make sure you
spell that with a Z!) so your HD won't get cluttered up.
